//? Title: DeepDream:visible bounded tensor optimization of original images
//? Requires: vanilla_saliency.mepml
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Frozen convolutional features can be amplified by changing an existing image. Start from genuine MNIST digits,show every image TensorSGD step,projection and backtracking trial across three octaves,and compare layer,initial-weight,single-scale and resize-only controls.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.11_interpretability/deepdream.cpp`.

> The method

Maximize a frozen layer's mean post-ReLUactivation by changing only the input. With ordinary input derivativeg,use a shared RMS-normalized ascent direction,project to bounded pixels,and backtrack on actual candidate objectives:

$$ x'=clip_{[0,1]}\left(x+\eta\frac{g}{\sqrt{mean(g^2)}+10^{-12}}\right). $$
\alttext(Add an RMS-normalized input gradient scaled by the candidate rate,then clip pixels to the unit interval;accept only nondecreasing actual feature scores.)

The report expresses ascent through plain tensorSGD on the negative normalized derivative. Classifier weights remain frozen;the mean feature objective differs from fitting a categorical loss. This small MNIST adaptation is not a pretrained Inception dream benchmark.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/deepdream_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/deepdream_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/deepdream_concept.tikz > build/deepdream_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/deepdream_concept.svg build/deepdream_concept.dvi > build/deepdream_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
