> Frozen features and genuine starting digits

Restore the exact selected and actual-initial MNIST arrays from
[vanilla saliency](vanilla_saliency.mepml),whose96explicit tensor Adam updates
and all held-out errors remain visible. No classifier parameter is optimized
here. Start from the same ten genuine held-out first-digit observations and
retain their source IDs. The optimized objects are image tensors,not model weights.

Maximize the mean of all post-ReLUconv2features,or conv1for a separate control.
Use20px,24px,28pxhalf-pixel octaves,five input steps at each. Resizing changes
the image and the feature lattice,so monotonicity is checked within each octave;
the first20pxscore and final28pxscore are not a same-input-scale comparison.
Actual main within-octave scores are.419970304to.536893606at20px,
.511448920to.654157698at24px,and.631932259to.779571593at28px.
The downward transitions between octaves are resampling effects and remain visible.
The shared RMS is over the entire image batch,not independently per digit.

> Executed tensor architecture

The diagram shows the forward MNIST CNN that the attribution or feature-optimization method inspects; the attribution algorithm is explained separately.

This figure executes the inference configuration shown in the code, using a zero-valued
shape probe without fitting or loading a checkpoint. Named stage boundaries group
whole subgraphs where available; other nodes retain functional-layer detail. Exact
batch-inclusive shapes and reachable parameter totals come from the trace. Shared
linear scales map spatial dimensions and channel counts to blocks; the one-pixel
visibility floor is disclosed in the legend. Labels use compact monospace text,
rotate counterclockwise and sit beside their own glyphs. Arrows flow left to right;
wide diagrams scroll at native size on the website.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deepdream_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::ParameterStore p(1103);
  n::Module         architecture_model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& image) { return m::SaliencyCnn(p, image).logits; },
      "DeepDream:visible bounded tensor optimization of original images");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.labels                = {.type = n::ModelPlotLabel::NameAndShape, .size = 12, .wrap = 24};
  options.spacing               = {.layer = 24, .lane = 12, .label = 8, .margin = 20};
  options.sizing.spatial_size   = 96;
  options.sizing.channel_size   = 42;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 1;
  options.opacity               = .8;
  const auto diagram            = architecture_model.plot(n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}), options);
  diagram.save_svg("build/deepdream_architecture.svg");
  std::print(
      "{} displayed nodes; {} reachable learned values.\n",
      diagram.nodes().size(),
      diagram.parameter_count());
}
