> Complete within-octave objective changes

Plot every before/after score separately for each octave;resampling can introduce
a discontinuity between the end of one octave and the next start. Positive
feature amplification is an optimization result,not improved classification,
realism or explanation quality. All input images,gradients,accepted rates and
backtracking counts remain in the local archive for replay.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/deepdream_scores.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto &[key, value] : n::load_npz("build/deepdream_outputs.npz"))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colors{{37, 99, 235}, {220, 38, 38}, {22, 163, 74}};
  std::print("| main octave | start score | final score |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int octave = 0; octave < 3; ++octave) {
    std::vector<n::Tensor> values{a.at("main_o" + std::to_string(octave) + "_s0_before").to(n::DType::Float64)};
    for (int step = 0; step < 5; ++step)
      values.push_back(
          a.at("main_o" + std::to_string(octave) + "_s" + std::to_string(step) + "_after"));
    std::print("| {} | {:.9g} | {:.9g} |\n", 20 + 4 * octave, values.front().item(),
               values.back().item());
    plot.lines(n::arange(0, 6).to_vector<double>(), n::stack(values, 0).to_vector<double>(),
               std::to_string(20 + 4 * octave) + "px", colors[octave]);
  }
  plot.title("Every main within-octave feature score")
      .x_label("local input step0..5")
      .y_label("mean post-ReLUconv2activation");
  plot.save_svg("build/deepdream_scores.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| main octave | start score | final score |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 20 | 0.419970304 | 0.536893606 |
| 24 | 0.51144892 | 0.654157698 |
| 28 | 0.631932259 | 0.779571593 |
\image(figures/deepdream_scores.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All three complete within-octave objective traces. Separate curves retain the actual resampling discontinuities;cross-scale start/final values are not presented as the same fixed optimization problem.)
\alttext(All three complete within-octave objective traces. Separate curves retain the actual resampling discontinuities;cross-scale start/final values are not presented as the same fixed optimization problem.)


> Conclusion

Every bounded image update and within-octave objective is explicit. Original digits and five actual controls distinguish feature amplification from classifier fitting and resizing. Increased activation alone does not establish realistic images,better recognition or causal explanation.

